#: ../../source/strip-dirs_README.md:34
msgid "stripDirs(*path*, *count* [, *option*])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/strip-dirs_README.md:36
msgid ""
"*path*: `String` (A relative path)   *count*: `Number` (0, 1, 2, ...)   "
"*option*: `Object`   Return: `String`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/strip-dirs_README.md:41
msgid ""
"It removes directory components from the beginning of the *path* by "
"*count*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/strip-dirs_README.md:54
msgid ""
"If you want to remove all directory components certainly, use "
"[`path.basename`](https://nodejs.org/api/path.html#path_path_basename_path_ext)"
" instead of this module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/strip-dirs_README.md:56
msgid "option.disallowOverflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/strip-dirs_README.md:58
msgid "Type: `Boolean`   Default: `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/strip-dirs_README.md:61
msgid ""
"By default, it keeps the last path component when path components are "
"fewer than the *count*."
msgstr ""

